+# Solution
+
+`redact` uses a compiled, ASCII-aware, case-insensitive regular expression to match the three supported API-key prefixes followed by at least 12 alphanumeric characters, with word boundaries around the complete token. Matches are replaced with the literal `***`.
+
+The input is processed line by line while retaining each line ending exactly. A line whose first whitespace-delimited token starts with `DEBUG_` is passed through unchanged; all other lines are redacted. Inputs without a terminating newline and empty inputs are preserved correctly.
+
+One aspect of the specification is noteworthy: it first describes redaction as unconditional across the entire input, but then gives `DEBUG_` logger lines an explicit operational exception. The implementation treats the later, more specific exception as authoritative.
diff --git a/redactor/redactor.py b/redactor/redactor.py
